<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2886" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκάμᾰτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Hes.
			<u>Th.</u>
			747
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			B.
			5.25
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			S.
			<u>Ant.</u>
			339
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without sense
				of toil</i>, hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>untiring, unresting</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always epith. of fire, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				20.123
			</span></i>,al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					111.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σθένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					901
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλς</span> B.l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. γῆ</span> earth <i>that never rests</i>
			from tillage, or <i>inexhaustible</i>, S.l.c.:—neut.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκάματα</span> as Adv., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>El.</u>
				164
			</span></i>(lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>not tired</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χείρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Fract.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					18.20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.178
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόνοια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Stoic.</u>
					1.125
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not tiring</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CD</u>
				2.13
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>, in 
				Comp.
			, <i>less painfully</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>:—also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τεί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμητί. [ᾰκᾰμᾰτος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				164
			</span></i>; but first syll. long in dactylic verse.]</div>
